% expect-output: null
% expect-output: --nostringval--
% expect-output: [null null]
% expect-output: -mark-
% Scenario: == writes null in its syntactic form, null, and = writes it
% as --nostringval--, since null has no text for cvs; an array of nulls
% prints each element the same way, while mark keeps its bracketed form.
null == null =
2 array ==
mark ==
